; RecipeTrail.inix -- how this database opens, and how each table is heard.
;
; ; Look is each table's default columns and prime its default order (5 November 2026); a table's
; saved columns, order and filter are written here only when a person chooses them, except an order
; that runs newest first, which prime cannot say.
; [Database] decides which table the window starts on. Each [Table:<name>]
; decides which fields the row speaks, in what order, and how the rows are
; sorted. DbDo writes these keys back whenever you change the columns, the sort
; or the filter, so what you adjust is remembered here.
;
; A row is heard, not seen, so the field that decides whether to keep listening
; comes first, and three fields is the target. The first field is also what
; first-letter navigation searches.
;
; The window opens on recipes. ingredients is the shared list they draw on.

[Database]

InitialTable = recipes

[Table:recipes]

; SelectFields, 13 October 2026: cuisine is nearly always the same, so it says little.
; OrderFields, 13 October 2026: grouped by course, as a cookbook is.

[Table:ingredients]

; OrderFields, 13 October 2026: grouped by where each sits in the store, as the shopping list is.

[Table:defs]


[Table:maps]

